Title: Test that Zotero.Prefs.get's second arg is read as the fully-qualified flag, not a default
Created: 2026-09-06
Author: sim

--- log ---
2026-09-06T15:33Z sim created

--- body ---

## Context

`bench/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js:34` reads the sitter's debug pref as
`Zotero.Prefs.get(DEBUG_PREF, true)`. Ticket 0698's SPEC.md documentation
(merged via PR #386) states this as fact: the second argument is the
"fully-qualified name" flag, not a default value, so an undeclared pref
reads `undefined`, `!undefined` is `true`, and the sitter treats trace-level
output as off by default.

This reading is backed by external Zotero API knowledge and the code's own
comment, but nothing in this repo independently establishes it. Every mock
`Zotero.Prefs.get` in `tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs` returns `true`
unconditionally, ignoring its arguments -- so the test suite cannot
distinguish the documented reading from the inverted one, under which the
second argument WOULD be a default and an undeclared pref would ship
debug-trace output ON by default. If the documented reading is wrong, SPEC.md
now states the opposite of shipped behavior and nothing catches it.

## Work

- Confirm the correct semantics of `Zotero.Prefs.get(name, global)` against
  real Zotero source (the installed `/opt/zotero7/app/omni.ja`, as other
  sitter tickets in this raid did) or Zotero's own documentation.
- Add a test that discriminates the two readings: a mock `Zotero.Prefs.get`
  that actually respects its arguments (returns `undefined`/throws for an
  undeclared pref name, distinct behavior for the flag vs. a default), and
  assert the sitter's trace-level gating behaves per the documented reading.

## Acceptance

- [ ] A test exists that would fail if `Zotero.Prefs.get`'s second argument
      were misread as a default value rather than the fully-qualified-name
      flag.
- [ ] SPEC.md's paragraph (R22 block, near "declared nowhere and reads as
      unset") is confirmed accurate, or corrected if the investigation finds
      otherwise.

## Scope

Small, code-only. Split from ticket 0698 (documentation-only) because this
requires a test/code change, which that ticket excluded.

